  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far (config_020, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted in a multiprofile multimodal setup. The progression config_002→config_016→config_010→config_020 shows consistent gains from upgrading each component (fusion→image encoder→aggregation). The RNA encoder has only been tested as scvi_n200 and pca_n2000 in this high-performing region, and scvi_n200 clearly outperformed pca_n2000. Question: config_045 tests scgpt (a generative-model-based RNA encoder) in the otherwise-identical best configuration (imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile). This is the single most informative untested variable in the top-performing region—scgpt could capture richer cell-type-specific gene expression patterns than scvi_n200's latent representation. Why this is the best next experiment: With 4 experiments remaining, exploiting the proven best architecture while exploring the one untested RNA encoder is the highest-expected-value move. If scgpt matches or beats scvi_n200, we gain a new best; if not, we confirm scvi_n200 is optimal and can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning. Expected cost: moderate—scgpt is likely slightly more expensive than scvi_n200, but the imagenet_vit_l + transformer combination has been among the cheapest (3.6–4.8 GPU hrs), so I estimate ~5–8 GPU hours, comparable to or slightly above config_020."
